 "result_text": "I changed the `dayfirst` default in `parse` from `True` to `False` (`delorean/interface.py`), so `2017-05-02` now reads as May 2nd. I checked it with `parse('2017-05-02 05:38:49')`, which returns 2017-05-02. I couldn't check your exact example. `parse('2017-05-02T05:38:49.899Z')` crashes in this environment with `'zoneinfo.ZoneInfo' object has no attribute 'localize'`. That error comes from the timezone handling in `delorean/dates.py`, and I didn't look into it or change it.\n\nThe cause was that `dayfirst=True` combined with `yearfirst=True` makes the underlying date parser read year-first strings as year-day-month.\n\nI also updated the sentence in `docs/quickstart.rst` that states the default. The precedence list below it still describes the `dayfirst=True` case first, so you may want to reorder it.\n\nI didn't run the test suite.",
